<title>FRANCE: MOTOR RACING-LE MANS 24-HOURS TIMES AFTER ONE HOUR.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-LE MANS 24-HOURS TIMES AFTER ONE HOUR.</headline>
<dateline>LE MANS, France 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading times after one</p>
<p>hour of the Le Mans 24 Hours race on Saturday:</p>
<p>1. Michele Alboreto (Italy)/Stephan Johansson (Sweden)/Tom</p>
<p>Kristensen (Denmark), Porsche-Joest 15 laps</p>
<p>2. Eric van de Poele (Belgium)/Riccardo Patrese (Italy)/Aguri</p>
<p>Suzuki (Japan), Nissan R390 0.644 seconds behind</p>
<p>3. Yannick Dalmas (France)/Ralf Kelleners (Germany)/Emmanuel</p>
<p>Collard (France), Porsche 911 GT1, 1.125 seconds</p>
<p>4. JJ Lehto (Finland)/Steve Soper (Britain)/Nelson Piquet</p>
<p>(Brazil), McLaren BMW F1GTR 2.633</p>
<p>5. Martin Brundle (Britain)/Wayne Taylor (South Africa)/Jorg</p>
<p>Muller (Germany), Nissan R390 17.275</p>
<p>6. Christophe Bouchut (France)/Andy Evans (U.S.)/Bertrand</p>
<p>Gachot (France), Porsche 911 GT1 19.100</p>
<p>7. Giampiero Moretti (Italy)/Didier Theys (Belgium)</p>
<p>/Massimiliano Papis (Italy), Ferrari 333 SP 24.349</p>
<p>8. Didier Cottaz (France)/Jerome Policand (France)/Marc Goosens</p>
<p>(Belgium), Courage C41 25.267</p>
<p>9. Hans Stuck (Germany)/Bob Wollek (France)/Thierry Boutsen</p>
<p>(Belgium), Porsche 911 GT1 27.791</p>
<p>10. Peter Kox (Netherlands)/Roberto Ravaglia (Italy)/Eric</p>
<p>Helary (France), McLaren BMW F1GTR 38.513</p>
</text>
